openmediavault-bcachefs (8.0.1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Use prebuilt kernel modules if available
  * Improve kernel module building
  * Don't report offline members as device files
  * Add a damaged files view
  * Fix encrypted filesystems never being reported as encrypted, and read
    their label and members without needing the passphrase
  * Fix Grow on the Filesystems page doing nothing; members whose device
    has grown are now resized
  * Quote the label, group names and targets when formatting, and validate
    them before any device is wiped
  * Scrub every member of a multi-device filesystem, not just one, and
    report files left damaged after the scrub
  * Only delete real subvolumes; never fall back to deleting files
  * Allow deleting snapshots from the Subvolumes page
  * Don't add the btrfs-only "ssd" mount option
  * Quote cron job arguments and escape "%" in job comments
  * Details no longer fails on encrypted filesystems; it shows the usage
    report when the superblock cannot be read without the passphrase
  * Add failure domains: per group at creation, per device when adding a
    device or from the Devices page, and a failure domain report in Usage
  * Add taking devices offline and bringing them back online; offline
    members are listed and can be removed
  * Add the write_degraded and missing_dev_timeout options
  * Auto-unlock no longer waits for member devices (wait-devices is a no-op
    in current bcachefs-tools) and reads the key file with unlock -f

 -- OpenMediaVault Plugin Developers <plugins@omv-extras.org>  Fri, 28 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

